k=o.xH(A.bz(!0,!0,!1)+" are the main way to organize your ideas. Each "+A.bz(!1,!1,!1)+" represents a type of activity or interest.\n\nExamples of "+A.bz(!0,!0,!1)+':\n\u2022 "Watch a Movie"\n\u2022 "Read a Book"\n\u2022 "Try a Restaurant"\n\u2022 "Learn a Skill"\n\u2022 "Visit a Place"\n\nWithin each '+A.bz(!1,!1,!1)+", you add individual "+A.bd(!1,!0,!1)+' - the specific things you want to do. For example, in "Watch a Movie", you might add "The Godfather", "Blade Runner", or "Spirited Away".\n\nYou can make your '+A.bz(!1,!0,!1)+" public to share with others, or keep them private for your eyes only.\n",a,1,"Compiling "+k)
s=o.xH("You can add links pointing to external resources for your "+A.bd(!1,!0,!1)+". This makes it easy to jump directly to relevant content.\n\nSupported link types:\n\u2022 Streaming services (Netflix, Amazon Prime, Apple TV+, etc.)\n\u2022 Music services (Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube Music, Tidal)\n\u2022 Websites and articles\n\u2022 Any other URL you want to save\n\nWhen you add a link, the app will try to automatically fetch information like titles and descriptions. For some services (like movies and music), it can even find where content is available to stream.\n\nPro tip: Just paste a URL into the headline when adding a new "+A.bd(!1,!1,!1)+", and the app will handle the rest!\n",a,2,"Linking Elsewhere")
